('112.5.b.7.A',3,'A ball thrown up in the air slows down and falls back. Which force pulls it down?','["gravity", "magnetism", "sound", "light"]'::jsonb,0,'Gravity pulls the ball back to Earth.','original'),
('112.5.b.7.A',3,'Which of these forces can act on an object without touching it?','["pushing a door", "gravity and magnetism", "kicking and throwing", "pushing and pulling by hand"]'::jsonb,1,'Gravity and magnetism can act from a distance.','original'),
('112.5.b.7.A',4,'Two magnets are placed near each other and move apart. What force is acting?','["heat pushing them apart", "friction pulling them together", "magnetic force pushing them apart", "gravity pulling them together"]'::jsonb,2,'Magnets can push each other away.','original'),
('112.5.b.7.B',2,'A student gives a swing a push. What changes about the swing?','["its weight", "its color", "its material", "its motion"]'::jsonb,3,'A push changes the motion of the swing.','original'),
