('112.5.b.7.B',3,'A student measures how far a toy car rolls after being pushed three times. What is the student measuring?','["the weight of the car", "the change in position", "the cost of the car", "the color of the car"]'::jsonb,1,'Distance traveled shows how the position changed.','original'),
('112.5.b.7.B',3,'A child pulls a wagon with a rope. Which way does the wagon move?','["it does not move", "straight up", "toward the child", "away from the child"]'::jsonb,2,'A pull moves an object toward the puller.','original'),
('112.5.b.7.B',3,'A rolling ball is stopped when a student presses a hand on it. What did the hand do?','["it made a magnet", "it made light", "it added gravity", "it changed the motion with a push"]'::jsonb,3,'A push can stop a moving object.','original'),
('112.5.b.7.B',2,'A student wants to make a ball roll faster. What should the student do?','["push it harder", "push it softly", "not push it", "pull it away slowly"]'::jsonb,0,'A harder push gives more speed.','original'),
('112.5.b.7.B',4,'A student records: push 1 moved a car 30 cm, push 2 moved it 60 cm, push 3 moved it 90 cm. What is the likely pattern?','["the car got lighter each time", "each push was stronger than the last", "each push was the same", "each push was weaker than the last"]'::jsonb,1,'More distance means a stronger push.','original'),
