('112.5.b.8.B',3,'A toy car moves slowly across a rug. A second moves quickly. Which has more mechanical energy?','["neither", "both the same", "the slow car", "the quick car"]'::jsonb,3,'A faster object has more mechanical energy.','original'),
('112.5.b.8.B',3,'A student releases a ball from a low height and then from a higher height. Which ball is going faster when it hits the floor?','["the ball dropped from higher", "they are the same", "neither one moves", "the ball dropped from lower"]'::jsonb,0,'A higher drop gives more speed.','original'),
('112.5.b.8.B',2,'A ball rolls slowly and then speeds up. What happens to its mechanical energy?','["it decreases", "it increases", "it stays the same", "it disappears"]'::jsonb,1,'A faster object has more mechanical energy.','original'),
('112.5.b.8.B',3,'A student tests how far a ball rolls from ramps of different heights. What does the student change?','["the room''s lights", "the day of the week", "the height of the ramp", "the color of the ball"]'::jsonb,2,'Ramp height changes the ball''s speed and energy.','original'),
('112.5.b.8.B',4,'A student records the ball''s speed on three ramps: 1 m/s, 2 m/s, 3 m/s. Which ramp gives the ball the most mechanical energy?','["the ramp with 2 m/s", "the ramp with 1 m/s", "they are all the same", "the ramp with 3 m/s"]'::jsonb,3,'Greater speed means more mechanical energy.','original'),
