('112.5.b.11.C',3,'Which material is made from recycled paper?','["a cardboard box", "a plastic toy", "a metal can", "a glass bottle"]'::jsonb,0,'Cardboard can be made from recycled paper.','original'),
('112.5.b.11.C',3,'A student uses a cloth bag instead of a new paper bag each time. What is this?','["littering", "reusing and reducing", "burning", "wasting"]'::jsonb,1,'A cloth bag is used again and reduces waste.','original'),
('112.5.b.11.C',3,'Which choice saves the most natural resources?','["use things once", "buy new items often", "reduce, reuse, and recycle", "throw away often"]'::jsonb,2,'These actions help conserve resources.','original'),
('112.5.b.11.C',4,'A school collects used paper and sends it to a plant that makes new paper. What does this save?','["plastic", "metal", "glass", "trees"]'::jsonb,3,'Recycling paper reduces the need to cut trees.','original'),
('112.5.b.12.A',2,'Some birds fly south for the winter. What is this called?','["migration", "metamorphosis", "hibernation", "dormancy"]'::jsonb,0,'Migration is moving to another place for the season.','original'),
('112.5.b.12.A',3,'A bear sleeps through much of the winter in a den. What is this called?','["dormancy", "hibernation", "migration", "pollination"]'::jsonb,1,'Hibernation is a long, deep sleep to survive winter.','original'),
('112.5.b.12.A',3,'Maple trees lose their leaves and stop growing in winter. What is this called?','["camouflage", "migration", "dormancy", "hibernation"]'::jsonb,2,'Plants rest in dormancy when it is cold.','original'),
('112.5.b.12.A',3,'Why do some animals migrate in the fall?','["to find colder weather", "to build ice dens", "to avoid all other animals", "to find warmer places with more food"]'::jsonb,3,'Cold temperatures reduce food supplies.','original'),
('112.5.b.12.A',3,'A desert plant stays dormant during a long dry period. What does this help it do?','["survive until rain returns", "make more shade", "move to a new place", "grow faster"]'::jsonb,0,'Dormancy saves water and energy.','original'),
('112.5.b.12.A',3,'Which animal is known for hibernating?','["a dolphin", "a bear", "a butterfly", "a goose"]'::jsonb,1,'Many bears hibernate in winter.','original'),
('112.5.b.12.A',4,'A spring with lots of rain makes many wildflowers grow. What does this show?','["rain stops plants from growing", "flowers prefer drought", "rain affects plant growth", "weather has no effect"]'::jsonb,2,'Precipitation helps plants grow.','original'),
('112.5.b.12.B',2,'Where does the energy in most food chains begin?','["the Moon", "wind", "rocks", "the Sun"]'::jsonb,3,'Plants use sunlight, and animals get energy from plants.','original'),
('112.5.b.12.B',3,'In the food chain sun → grass → grasshopper → frog, what does the frog get energy from?','["eating the grasshopper", "the Sun directly", "the grass directly", "the water only"]'::jsonb,0,'The frog gets its energy by eating the grasshopper.','original'),
('112.5.b.12.B',3,'All the frogs are removed from a pond. What may happen to the insects the frogs ate?','["the insects will turn into frogs", "there may be more insects", "nothing will change", "there may be fewer insects"]'::jsonb,1,'Without frogs eating them, insect numbers may grow.','original'),
('112.5.b.12.B',3,'All the bees disappear from a field of flowers. What might happen to the plants?','["more seeds will be made", "nothing will change", "fewer seeds may be made", "plants will move"]'::jsonb,2,'Bees help pollinate flowers.','original'),
('112.5.b.12.B',3,'Which living thing is a PRODUCER?','["a hawk", "a rabbit", "a snake", "grass"]'::jsonb,3,'Grass makes its own food.','original'),
('112.5.b.12.B',3,'Which shows a food chain in the correct order, starting with the producer?','["seeds → mouse → snake → hawk", "mouse → seeds → snake → hawk", "hawk → snake → mouse → seeds", "snake → hawk → seeds → mouse"]'::jsonb,0,'Energy starts with the producer and passes to each consumer in order.','original'),
('112.5.b.12.B',4,'Fish in a lake eat small water insects. If the insects are poisoned, what may happen to the fish?','["the fish will become insects", "the fish may have less food", "nothing will happen", "the fish will have more food"]'::jsonb,1,'Animals depend on the organisms they eat.','original'),
('112.5.b.12.C',2,'A long drought dries up a pond. What may happen to the fish there?','["they will multiply faster", "they will turn into frogs", "they may die or the pond life must move", "they will grow bigger"]'::jsonb,2,'Fish need water to live.','original'),
('112.5.b.12.C',3,'A flood washes away a field of plants. What may happen to the animals that depended on them?','["they will turn into plants", "they will stay and grow bigger", "they will find more food there", "they may move away to find food"]'::jsonb,3,'Animals may relocate if food is gone.','original'),
('112.5.b.12.C',3,'After a flood, new plants grow in the soil left behind. Which organisms benefit?','["plants that like wet, rich soil", "no plants", "desert plants only", "plants that need no water"]'::jsonb,0,'Flood deposits can enrich soil.','original'),
('112.5.b.12.C',3,'During a drought, which plant is most likely to survive?','["a fern", "a cactus", "a water lily", "a moss"]'::jsonb,1,'A cactus stores water.','original'),
('112.5.b.12.C',3,'Why might frogs thrive after a wet season?','["there is less water", "there are fewer insects", "there are more ponds to live and breed in", "there are fewer plants"]'::jsonb,2,'More water gives frogs more places to live.','original'),
('112.5.b.12.C',3,'A drought makes grass turn brown. What might the deer that eat grass do?','["turn into plants", "eat rocks", "grow wings", "move to a new area with food"]'::jsonb,3,'Animals move to find food.','original'),
('112.5.b.12.C',4,'Which natural change could cause some organisms to perish?','["a long flood or drought", "a sunny afternoon", "a gentle breeze", "a light rain shower"]'::jsonb,0,'Extreme changes can harm living things.','original'),
('112.5.b.12.D',2,'What is a fossil?','["a new plant", "the remains or traces of a living thing from long ago", "a kind of weather", "a modern animal"]'::jsonb,1,'Fossils are preserved evidence of past life.','original'),
('112.5.b.12.D',3,'A fossil of a fish is found in the desert. What does this suggest?','["fish fell from the sky", "the desert was always dry", "the area was once covered by water", "fish live in deserts"]'::jsonb,2,'A fish fossil shows water used to be there.','original'),
('112.5.b.12.D',3,'Where are fossils usually found?','["in clouds", "in puddles", "in the air", "in layers of rock"]'::jsonb,3,'Fossils are preserved in sedimentary rock.','original'),
('112.5.b.12.D',3,'What can a scientist learn from a fossil leaf?','["what plants lived there long ago", "what time it is", "what the weather is today", "how fast a car goes"]'::jsonb,0,'Fossils show past life.','original'),
('112.5.b.12.D',3,'Which is a fossil found in Texas?','["a new bird nest", "a dinosaur footprint", "a modern cactus", "a tire track"]'::jsonb,1,'Texas has dinosaur tracks, including at Dinosaur Valley State Park.','original'),
('112.5.b.12.D',3,'Which fossils might be found in a limestone rock that was once an ocean floor?','["tree trunks", "grass blades", "seashells", "cactus spines"]'::jsonb,2,'Ocean animals leave fossil shells.','original'),
('112.5.b.12.D',4,'A scientist finds fossil ferns in a dry area. What does this tell about long ago?','["the area was always dry", "the area was snowy", "ferns grow in deserts", "the area was wetter then"]'::jsonb,3,'Ferns need moist places.','original'),
('112.5.b.13.A',2,'A giraffe has a long neck. How does this help it survive?','["it can reach leaves high in trees", "it can hide in grass", "it can dig", "it can swim"]'::jsonb,0,'A long neck reaches food high in trees.','original'),
('112.5.b.13.A',2,'A duck has webbed feet. How does this help it?','["it can climb trees", "it can paddle through water", "it can run fast on land", "it can dig burrows"]'::jsonb,1,'Webbed feet push against water.','original'),
('112.5.b.13.A',3,'A cheetah has long, strong legs. How does this help it?','["it can climb walls", "it can fly", "it can run fast to catch prey", "it can swim"]'::jsonb,2,'Long legs help it sprint.','original'),
('112.5.b.13.A',3,'A porcupine has sharp quills. How do they help it?','["they help it fly", "they help it swim", "they help it see in the dark", "they protect it from predators"]'::jsonb,3,'Quills defend against attackers.','original'),
('112.5.b.13.A',3,'A sloth has long, strong claws. How do they help it?','["they let it hang from tree branches", "they let it dig deep tunnels", "they let it swim", "they let it fly"]'::jsonb,0,'Claws hold branches.','original'),
('112.5.b.13.A',3,'An owl has large eyes. How do large eyes help it?','["it can swim", "it can see well at night", "it can hear less", "it can smell better"]'::jsonb,1,'Large eyes gather more light in the dark.','original'),
('112.5.b.13.A',4,'A hummingbird has a long, thin beak. What does this structure help it do?','["catch fish", "crack open nuts", "reach nectar deep inside flowers", "dig for worms"]'::jsonb,2,'A long thin beak fits deep into flowers.','original'),
('112.5.b.13.B',2,'A beetle has four stages: egg, larva, pupa, adult. This is called what?','["migration", "no change", "incomplete metamorphosis", "complete metamorphosis"]'::jsonb,3,'Four stages means complete metamorphosis.','original'),
('112.5.b.13.B',3,'A cricket nymph looks like a small adult cricket. Which type of life cycle does it have?','["incomplete metamorphosis", "no life cycle", "plant cycle", "complete metamorphosis"]'::jsonb,0,'Incomplete metamorphosis has egg, nymph, and adult stages.','original'),
('112.5.b.13.B',3,'A lima bean seed is planted. Which stage comes next?','["it becomes fruit first", "a seedling sprouts", "it becomes a seed again", "it becomes a flower first"]'::jsonb,1,'A seed sprouts into a seedling.','original'),
('112.5.b.13.B',3,'Which is the correct order for a radish plant?','["seedling, seed, adult plant", "adult plant, seed, seedling", "seed, seedling, adult plant, seed", "seed, adult plant, seedling"]'::jsonb,2,'Plants grow from seed to seedling to adult and make new seeds.','original'),
('112.5.b.13.B',3,'How is a beetle larva different from an adult beetle?','["the larva looks the same", "the larva is larger", "the larva has wings", "the larva looks very different"]'::jsonb,3,'In complete metamorphosis, larvae differ from adults.','original'),
('112.5.b.13.B',3,'What is the last stage of a beetle''s life cycle?','["adult", "pupa", "egg", "larva"]'::jsonb,0,'The adult is the final stage.','original'),
('112.5.b.13.B',4,'A student compares a bean plant and a beetle. What do both have?','["the same number of stages", "a life cycle with stages", "wings", "no changes"]'::jsonb,1,'All living things go through a life cycle.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Science' and d.language = 'en'
